# Everything here is cloned onto Ubuntu and executed there.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows produces CRLF line endings, and a shell
# script with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" —
# a message that names the wrong problem and costs a class twenty minutes. It
# is also invisible in every editor and every diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
